{# A body region inside a screen — the IA's own word for it. A screen puts one or
   more of these into `canvas.main`: an optional heading, optional right-aligned
   actions, and a content container whose direct children are the cells.

   IT SUPERSEDES `section`, WITH THREE CONCERNS DELIBERATELY DROPPED.
     * ONE `inset` instead of `padding_x` + `padding_y`. On `section` the same
       word meant two sizes — `sm` was 10px across and 8px down — so a caller
       who set both to `sm` got an asymmetric box and no way to see why.
     * `direction: row` instead of `justify_items`. A grid cell BLOCKIFIES its
       child, so an `inline-flex` pill became a full-width rounded rectangle and
       a list of labels rendered as a column of them. A wrapping row keeps its
       children's intrinsic widths by construction, which is the only thing
       `justify_items: start` was ever used for.
     * NO `header_style`. A zone heading has one style, so two adjacent zones
       cannot disagree about what a zone heading looks like.

   A ZONE WITH NOTHING TO SHOW RENDERS NOTHING AT ALL — no <section>, no heading,
   no empty grid (BB-414). "Something to show" is CONTENT, ACTIONS or a
   DESCRIPTION; a heading alone is not, because a heading is a label FOR
   something and a label over nothing is a promise the screen does not keep. The
   two cases that forced this are both on the ticket detail and both used to
   render as a heading over an empty box: the About zone on a ticket with no
   description, and the Run history zone whose rows are all invisible to the
   reader.

   THE DESCRIPTION COUNTS, and leaving it out was a real defect rather than a
   nuance (BB-414, second review gate). `description` is a PROP and not a
   slot, so it is not part of `content_content`, and a zone carrying a heading
   and a description but no content dropped the description with everything
   else — prose the reader was meant to read, gone with the empty box it was
   supposed to explain. It is not a label for something absent the way a heading
   is; it is a sentence, and a sentence is content. The project and settings
   screens are the surfaces this is latent for.

   THE PROBE STRIPS TAGS BEFORE IT TESTS, and that is not tidiness. With
   `twig.config.debug` on — every DDEV site — SDC wraps EVERY component in
   `<!-- 🥚 Component start/end -->`, so a child component that rendered nothing
   still arrives here as 91 bytes. A bare `|trim is not empty` would therefore
   keep the zone in development and drop it in production, which is the one
   outcome worse than either. `|striptags` removes comments as well as tags, and
   the allow-list keeps the void elements that ARE content without carrying text,
   so an icon-only or input-only zone still counts as filled.

   `<drupal-render-placeholder>` IS IN THAT ALLOW-LIST FOR THE SAME REASON AS
   `<input>`, and its absence was the probe's second defect (BB-414, second
   review gate). Anything Drupal defers — a #lazy_builder, a form, a block whose
   render is cached, the messages area — reaches this template as that single
   placeholder element and NOTHING else: no text, no void element, no attribute
   a `striptags` survives. So a zone whose only content was a form was measured
   as empty and dropped, and the placeholder would have been replaced with the
   real markup a moment later during rendering. Content that has not been built
   yet is still content.

   ACTIONS COUNT AS CONTENT, deliberately: a zone whose list is empty but which
   owns an "Add" affordance is the one place a reader can put the first item into
   it, and hiding that would hide the way out of the empty state.

   THE HEADING IS AN h2. `page_header` owns the screen's only h1 (D5); this is
   the level below it. A zone with nothing in its heading slot renders no heading
   element at all rather than an empty one.

   SPACING IS THE TOKEN SCALE (D16). `inset` and `gap` resolve to `space-*` and
   nothing else — no arbitrary pixel value appears in this template.

   `inset` PADS VERTICALLY ONLY. The horizontal edge belongs to the `canvas` /
   `page_header` (`px-group`, `xl:px-gutter`) or to the `surface_card` a carded
   zone sits in, so a zone never adds a second left edge inside them.

   Both the heading and the actions are CAPTURED before they are tested, so a
   slot filled through a `{% block %}` override still renders its wrapper: a
   wrapper written inside the block would be replaced wholesale by the fill. #}
{% set inset_map = {
  'none': '',
  'sm': 'py-stack',
  'md': 'py-group',
  'lg': 'py-gutter',
} %}
{% set gap_map = {
  'none': 'gap-0',
  'sm': 'gap-zone-sm',
  'md': 'gap-zone-md',
  'lg': 'gap-zone-lg',
  'section': 'gap-section',
} %}
{% set col_map = {
  1: 'grid-cols-1',
  2: 'grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2',
  3: 'grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3',
  4: 'grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4',
} %}
{% set gap_class = gap_map[gap|default('md')]|default(gap_map['md']) %}
{#- `min-w-0` lets a zone placed as a grid or flex cell shrink below its
    content's intrinsic width instead of overflowing the track. `align:
    center` centres the heading, the copy and the cells: a short result (a
    heading, a sentence, one action) standing alone in a card. #}
{% set centered = align|default('start') == 'center' %}
{% set zone_classes = ['flex', 'flex-col', 'min-w-0', 'gap-stack', (inset_map[inset|default('md')] ?? inset_map['md'])]|merge(centered ? ['items-center', 'text-center'] : []) %}
{#- `fill` is ONE row for a field and its submit: the first cell takes the
    remaining width, every later cell keeps its intrinsic width on one line, and
    all of them sit on the bottom edge so the button lines up with the input
    rather than with the field's label. It wraps only when the row cannot fit:
    the first cell's basis is the point below which it would rather move the
    later cells onto a new line than shrink further, and `max-w-full` keeps a
    wrapped cell (a select sized to its longest option) inside the row. #}
{% set content_classes = {
  'row': ['flex', 'flex-row', 'flex-wrap', 'items-start', gap_class],
  'fill': ['flex', 'flex-row', 'flex-wrap', 'items-end', gap_class, '*:first:flex-1', '*:first:basis-40', '*:first:min-w-0', '*:not-first:shrink-0', '*:not-first:max-w-full', '*:not-first:whitespace-nowrap'],
}[direction|default('column')] ?? ['grid', col_map[columns|default(1)]|default('grid-cols-1'), gap_class]|merge(centered ? ['justify-items-center'] : []) %}
{% set heading_content %}{% block heading %}{{ heading }}{% endblock %}{% endset %}
{% set actions_content %}{% block actions %}{{ actions }}{% endblock %}{% endset %}
{#- The content is CAPTURED like the other two, and for one more reason on top of
    the block-override one: it has to be tested before the wrapper is opened, and
    a `{% block %}` cannot be read twice. The wrapper stays OUTSIDE the block —
    the captured value is printed inside the grid below, so a slot filled through
    an override still gets its container. #}
{#- `is not empty`, not a truthy test: integer 0 is content (a reported load of
    0, an occupancy of 0) and `{% if content %}` drops it because Twig casts 0
    to false. The emptiness test below still hides a zone with nothing to show. #}
{% set content_content %}{% block content %}{% if content is not empty %}{{ content }}{% endif %}{% endblock %}{% endset %}
{#- The void elements that are content without being text, plus Drupal's
    placeholder for content it has not built yet. Everything else — including
    SDC's debug comments — is stripped before the emptiness test. #}
{% set visible_tags = '<img><svg><iframe><video><canvas><input><hr><progress><audio><drupal-render-placeholder>' %}
{% set shows_content = content_content|striptags(visible_tags)|trim is not empty %}
{% set shows_actions = actions_content|striptags(visible_tags)|trim is not empty %}
{% if shows_content or shows_actions or description %}
<section{{ (attributes ?: create_attribute()).addClass(zone_classes) }}>
  {% if heading_content|trim is not empty or description or actions_content|trim is not empty %}
    <div class="flex flex-col items-start gap-stack sm:flex-row sm:items-center">
      {#- THE SUB-LINE IS A PROP, NOT MARKUP IN THE HEADING SLOT. Ten block headers
          in the delivered scenes carry one, and with no prop for it they were
          written as block-level `<span>`s with inline `style=""` — the only thing
          that works from a scene file, because scene YAML is outside the CSS
          build's source paths. Declared here it is styled once, in the same
          treatment `page_header` gives the screen's sub-line, and it stays out of
          the heading. No `truncate`: a block sub-line is a sentence and wraps. #}
      {% if heading_content|trim is not empty or description %}
        <div class="flex flex-col min-w-0">
          {% if heading_content|trim is not empty %}
            <h2 data-zone-heading class="m-0 min-w-0 text-title {{ heading_size|default('section') == 'display' ? 'text-page-title font-display' : 'text-section-title' }}">{{ heading_content }}</h2>
          {% endif %}
          {% if description %}
            <p class="m-0 text-meta text-text-faint">{{ description }}</p>
          {% endif %}
        </div>
      {% endif %}
      {% if actions_content|trim is not empty %}
        <div class="sm:ml-auto flex items-center gap-stack shrink-0">{{ actions_content }}</div>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  {% endif %}
  <div class="{{ content_classes|join(' ')|trim }}"{% if list %} role="list"{% endif %}>{{ content_content }}</div>
</section>
{% endif %}
